          "facial_dialogue": {
            "verdict": "pass",
            "notes": "I inspected the visible mouth choices, blinks, gaze offsets, brow reactions and head motion independently of the body. Luma speaks as both characters start together and leave to screen right. The authored start prevents the earlier planted-foot slide. The foreground tree overlaps the departing cast intentionally, and both are outside the frame at the end. Mouth choices are manually editable approximations; the small eye-patch offsets communicate limited gaze rather than full eye rotation. This is a visual acting decision for the pilot, not a claim of auditory or phoneme-accurate performance review.",
